    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters May 8th with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **James Wood** serving as our anchor plays, both topping the 72-point threshold. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a favorable matchup against Montero, benefiting from an 11% boost due to SP skill and a strong platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is our premier leadoff option; his 72.30 score is bolstered by a massive 19% SP skill advantage against Snelling and a top-of-the-order boost that maximizes his potential for runs. **Josh Naylor** and **Seiya Suzuki** also provide reliable mid-tier production, with **Seiya Suzuki** benefiting from a slow delivery matchup that keeps his SB potential in play despite the lack of a platoon advantage.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with our core speed threats due to elite defensive backstops. **Corbin Carroll** remains a start at 57.90, but his projection is suppressed by a 2% penalty for facing a sub-1.90s pop-time catcher, even against a tough arm in McLean. We are keeping a close watch on **Brice Turang** (50.97); while his speed is vital, he faces an uphill battle against Fried, which limits his efficiency. Our most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 40.02 score. Ultimately, the projection favored the cumulative floor of our starters over **Kyle Karros**, as the negative impact of his 7th-hole placement and an elite opposing catcher nullified his park-adjusted upside. \n\nRisk management remains paramount as we navigate today\u2019s slate, particularly with the bottom of our order. **Gabriel Moreno**, **Austin Riley**, and **Jose Caballero** all hover near the 41\u201343 point range, largely due to the difficult SP skill profiles of McLean, Sheehan, and Misiorowski. We are keeping **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Mickey Moniak** on the bench, with **Giancarlo Stanton** confirmed out on the IL. With no extreme weather threats forecasted, our focus is squarely on maintaining our efficiency metrics while hoping the dynamic platoon advantages for **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** translate into high-impact run production.",
